# Optional project instructions for Codex

Use $dispatch for bounded parallel work. Validate exactly one nonempty TASK,
FILES, BAR, and RETURN field before dispatch. Free-text notes may follow them.
Use spawn_agent with agent_type, a stable task_name, message, and fork_turns="none".
Omit model and reasoning_effort; the installed role TOML pins those defaults.

Use seat-sweep for evidence, seat-exec for isolated implementation, and a fresh
seat-judge to check every result. Create or assign separate Git worktrees before
concurrent edits. Preserve unrelated work.

Keep task_name and the base role stable across retries. Execution rounds one and
two use seat-exec. Round three explicitly uses seat-exec-up. Round four returns
to the owner. Do not rename tasks or switch role families to evade the ladder.

The Codex hook checks visible roles and task names. It cannot inspect the encrypted
brief message: the dispatch skill and role instructions must check its format.
Review and trust new or changed Codex hooks before relying on routing. Use router
off, router on, and router status for the same switch as Claude Code.
